@import com.example.septic.web.RecordHelpEntry

<section class="state-records-outcomes" id="indiana-record-search-guide" aria-labelledby="indiana-record-search-title">
    <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">Make the county search useful</span>
        <h2 id="indiana-record-search-title">What are you trying to find in the Indiana file?</h2>
        <p>Indiana's local health departments handle residential septic permitting. Start with the property's county; a state program page is not a property-specific permit result.</p>
        <div>
            <details open>
                <summary>The tank or drain field location</summary>
                <p>Ask for the site sketch, as-built, or installation drawing tied to the address and parcel. Compare the building and lot with your property. A permit number alone does not show where to dig.</p>
                <p><a href="/septic-as-built-records/#layout-case" data-track-click="nav" data-track-source-context="indiana_layout_case" data-track-target-type="case_study">See how we read a historical layout in Roane County, Tennessee →</a></p>
            </details>
            <details open>
                <summary>An older file that the first search missed</summary>
                <p>Keep the tax parcel number, earlier owner names, old road names, and subdivision or lot clues. Ask the local office whether older files use different identifiers before assuming no record exists.</p>
                <p><a href="/septic-permit-search-by-address/#old-address-case" data-track-click="nav" data-track-source-context="indiana_old_address_case" data-track-target-type="case_study">Follow an older-address search in Overton County, Tennessee →</a></p>
            </details>
            <details open>
                <summary>The right county request route</summary>
                <p>Some counties publish a request form; others need office contact. Use the local instructions for copies of an existing file, rather than applying for a new septic permit.</p>
                <p><a href="/septic-records-checklist/indiana/st-joseph-county/" data-track-click="nav" data-track-source-context="indiana_local_route" data-track-target-type="county_records_page">St. Joseph County's records request</a> · <a href="/septic-records-checklist/indiana/monroe-county/" data-track-click="nav" data-track-source-context="indiana_local_route" data-track-target-type="county_records_page">Monroe County's file-contact route</a> · <a href="#county-pages">Choose another Indiana county</a></p>
            </details>
        </div>
        <p>These real investigations show how we work, not Indiana-specific rules or a promise that your property has the same records.</p>
        <p><a class="button button--primary" href="${RecordHelpEntry.of("missing").link("/septic-records-checklist/indiana/", "IN", null)}" data-record-help-cta data-track-click="nav" data-track-source-context="indiana_practical_guide_help" data-track-target-type="lead_form">Let us continue my Indiana record search →</a></p>
        <p>Get the records we locate and our explanation, free. Agency fees require your approval. For current condition or an exact on-site location, a field professional may still be needed.</p>
        <p><small>Official context: <a href="https://www.in.gov/health/eph/onsite-sewage-systems-program/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Indiana Onsite Sewage Systems Program</a> · <a href="https://secure.in.gov/health/eph/local-health-departments/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Local health department responsibilities</a>.</small></p>
    </div>
</section>
